# Execute individually with an HTTP client that preserves cookies.
# Use an existing test account; do not commit real credentials or tokens.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@email = 20260001@bjtu.edu.cn
@password = Hall12345!
@csrfToken = replace_with_csrf_data_token
@diningHallId = replace_with_id_from_dining_halls_response

### 1. Get anonymous CSRF token; preserve the response Cookie.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/csrf

### 2. Update csrfToken from step 1, then login.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{ "account": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 3. List active dining halls using the login Cookie. GET needs no CSRF header.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dining-halls
Accept: application/json

### 4. Set diningHallId above to an active hall ID from step 3, then list its active stalls.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dining-halls/{{diningHallId}}/stalls
Accept: application/json
